-- title:
--   Unique expansions along a lifted residue-field basis
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ be a noetherian local commutative ring with residue field $k =$ `IsLocalRing.ResidueField B`, and let $n, d$ be natural numbers. Let $\rho : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to B[\![x_1,\dots,x_n]\!]$ be a family of multivariate power series in $n$ variables over $B$ such that each $\rho_i$ has zero constant coefficient, such that for some $N$ every variable satisfies $X_i^N \in (\rho_1,\dots,\rho_n)$, and such that the quotient $C = B[\![x]\!]/(\rho_1,\dots,\rho_n)$ by the ideal generated by the range of $\rho$ is a finite $B$-module. Let $b : \mathrm{Fin}\,d \to B[\![x]\!]$ and let $\beta$ be a basis of the $k$-module $k \otimes_B C$ indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,d$ whose $j$-th member is $1 \otimes \bar b_j$, the image of $b_j$ in $C$ tensored with $1$. Then for every $f \in B[\![x]\!]$ there is a unique family $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,d \to B[\![y_1,\dots,y_n]\!]$ with $f = \sum_{j} \mathrm{subst}_{\rho}(c_j)\, b_j$, substitution of $\rho$ into $c_j$ being legitimate because the $\rho_i$ have no constant term.
--
--   This is the statement that $B[\![x_1,\dots,x_n]\!]$ is free of rank $d$ over the subring obtained by substituting $\rho$, with the prescribed family $b$ as basis: each $f$ has one and only one expansion $\sum_j c_j(\rho)\,b_j$. The form with an arbitrary lift $b$ of a residue-field basis is what the construction of bases for finite quotients of power series rings over a local ring and the study of substitution into multivariate formal group laws use.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPowerSeries_existsUnique_eq_sum_subst_mul_of_basis_residueField_tensor_quotient.lean

